{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content docs/work/active/wi-1002/WI-1002-parked-resume-skips-blocked.md; Get-Content docs/rubrics/kit-change-review.md; git diff f28530899cb1ceeb4bb0b1378ec8d288dc2bf32b...c873dcf8aade6179d893f6138adca8eefea9ab5c -- . ':(exclude)docs/iteration' ':(exclude)docs/reviews' ':(exclude)docs/log.md' ':(exclude)docs/log.d' ':(exclude)PROJECT_STATE.html' ':(exclude)docs/open-items.html' ':(exclude)docs/stage'; rg -n 'change.intake|Review threat model|Consolidate|When a guard|\"'^## [356]'\"' project-trajectory/PROCESS.md\"","aggregated_output":"+++\r\nid = \"WI-1002\"\r\ntitle = \"The dispatcher's parked-lane resume leaves out a lane whose claimed row reads blocked, so a filed owner-held step launches no worker\"\r\nworkstream = \"process\"\r\nsr_refs = [\"SR-026\", \"SR-148\"]\r\nspecref = \"docs/reviews/wi-993/012-ADJUDICATE-26b4d09.md\"\r\nbuildtier = \"medium\"\r\nsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\r\nplanmode = \"none\"\r\npriority = 5\r\n+++\r\n\r\n## Context\r\n\r\nFiled on trunk at WI-993's landing, from the SUCCESSOR ruling of its gate's\r\ndispute sitting (`docs/reviews/wi-993/012-ADJUDICATE-26b4d09.md`, finding PARK,\r\nre-graded MINOR there). `dispatch._parked_branches` reads no schedule, so on the\r\nunattended route a claimed row citing a pending item is relaunched, against the\r\nworker brief's \"no worker assignment\". The state predates WI-993, which only\r\nsanctions it. The fix reads the `blocked` disposition LLR-288 already derives; it\r\nadds no second predicate and no detector for a session that stopped and filed\r\nnothing (WI-993's call 7). LLR-143 owes its amendment and sitting. Owes its scope\r\ncritique before its claim.\r\n\r\n## Done-when\r\n\r\n- [ ] The parked-lane resume leaves out a lane whose claimed row reads blocked in\r\n      the shared schedule: it launches no worker, keeps the claim, goes on to\r\n      claim the next ready row and ends without a stall. A parked lane whose\r\n      claimed row reads anything else keeps today's resume admission. The\r\n      promise reaches supported workflows and the kit's own routes, as\r\n      PROCESS.md §6 \"Review threat model\" bounds a spec's promise; hand-edited\r\n      kit-written state, hand-chosen aliases and sub-second timing windows are\r\n      outside it.\r\n- [ ] The resume LLR is amended to say so.\r\n- [ ] A `tests/test_dispatch.py` case over a parked blocked lane beside a ready\r\n      row asserts no launch, the claim kept and the next row claimed.\r\n- [ ] RESYNC entry, if the behaviour reaches adopters.\r\n- [ ] Review bar: A+B (REVIEW-A plus an independent REVIEW-B).\r\n\r\n## Critique dispositions\r\n\r\nRound 1 (fresh Codex session, 2026-11-07): CHANGES-REQUESTED, two MINORs.\r\n\r\n- **S3, the default for other dispositions and the supported-workflow bound:\r\n  adopted.** The first Done-when item now reads \"A parked lane whose claimed\r\n  row reads anything else keeps today's resume admission\", and it carries the\r\n  bound.\r\n- **S4, the planning ruling: adopted as `planmode = \"none\"`.** The change is\r\n  one filter on the parked-lane list, reading a disposition that already\r\n  exists, and the Done-when's `tests/test_dispatch.py` case fully specifies it,\r\n  which is S4's stated exception.\r\n\r\nRound 2 (fresh Codex session, confirming, 2026-11-07): APPROVE, no findings; both dispositions confirmed.\r\n# Rubric — Reviewing a change to this kit (WI-852)\r\n\r\n**Adjudicates:** the checks a review of a change to this repository owes beyond\r\nthe kit's reviewer brief, which already asks for the failure classes, the\r\nDone-when coverage map, the red-before test, the unrepresentable clause and the\r\nrequirement-row sweep.\r\n**Used by:** an independent reviewer of a lane, when its brief is rendered with\r\n`review_brief.py review --rubric docs/rubrics/kit-change-review.md`.\r\n\r\n## Intent\r\n\r\nThe rules this repository holds its own lanes to (`CLAUDE.md`, and the owner\r\nrulings the spine-authoring skill records) that the kit's shipped brief cannot\r\nname, because an adopter's repository has its own.\r\n\r\n## Anchors\r\n\r\n**K1 — Requirement text is true, and the right way round.** Read every added or\r\namended SN, SR, LLR and TC cell against PROCESS.md and the code. *Bad:* a row\r\nstating the inverse of the rule its code implements; earlier waves shipped\r\nthat, and code review missed it.\r\n\r\n**K2 — Owner ruling R2, as review-churn ruling 5 refines it.** No SN or SR\r\ncell names an implementation carrier (a script, command, file or function),\r\nacceptance included. Current-carrier evidence lives in the TC rows that verify\r\nthe row, and a shipped boundary artifact (a registry, template, config file or\r\nlauncher) may be named at the LLR and TC tiers only. An approved cell keeps its\r\napproved text, names included, until it is amended through its authority.\r\n\r\n**K3 — Back-links and approved rows.** Each `Implements:` tag names the LLR\r\nwhose `module` is that file, and the function appears in that LLR's\r\n`code_symbol`. An approved row changes only where the spec grants it, and no\r\nStatus flips.\r\n\r\n**B1 — A finding stated as a guess.** Report a finding as a claim confirmed by\r\nreading or running the code, never as a guess.\r\ndiff --git a/docs/decisions/wi-1002.toml b/docs/decisions/wi-1002.toml\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..3194c924a\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/decisions/wi-1002.toml\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+# docs/decisions/wi-1002.toml — delegated calls in WI-1002's lane.\n+# Format: project-trajectory/decisions.template.toml.\n+\n+high_risk = []\n+\n+[decision.D-001]\n+decided = \"The tests-first commit adds two `tests/test_dispatch.py` cases over a fixture with a parked lane whose claimed row cites a pending item beside a ready row: the blocked lane draws no worker, keeps its claim, and the ready row