h the session dials forwarded), merges each finished branch through the serial merge slot (integrate.integrate) counting the WIs merged, and stops loudly on any composed refusal once the live lanes drain - a stall aborts, an empty frontier drains to exit 0. A NEEDS-HUMAN worker does not stop the run: its lane hands back (the WI closes partial and merges) and the run drives on; an active/ directory with no branch ref is residue, not a refusal. The session-config preflight applies only when work needs a worker. Never pushes.\"\"\"\n+detail = \"\"\"The scheduling front end a plain agent_loop.py launch runs, serial at lanes=1 (the lanes dial admits more lanes at once; each lane's mechanics are LLR-150's): each cycle re-derives the ready frontier (schedule.frontier), stops claiming under the tracked pause (a parked or finished lane still resumes and merges, and the run exits 8 once nothing is in flight), refuses on a dirty trunk at the cycle top while no lane is live (a change confined to agent_common.OWNER_ONLY_PATHS, the owner's scratchpad, is not dirt), resumes a parked claimed branch else claims the next queued WI in build order (integrate.claim, branch name check-ref-format-validated), launches one worker session on the claimed branch's worktree (agent_loop.py --worktree --wi with the session dials forwarded), merges each finished branch through the serial merge slot (integrate.integrate) counting the WIs merged, and stops loudly on any composed refusal once the live lanes drain - a stall aborts, an empty frontier drains to exit 0. A NEEDS-HUMAN worker does not stop the run: its lane hands back (the WI closes partial and merges) and the run drives on; an active/ directory with no branch ref is residue, not a refusal. A parked claimed branch whose claimed row reads blocked in the shared schedule is left out of resume: it launches no worker, keeps its claim, and the next ready row is claimed; the excluded lane does not count as a stall. A parked lane whose claimed row